<%- /*
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Lusoris <lusoris@pm.me>
SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2

Caller of the shared merge train, kept once in the fleet's operations
repository as .github/workflows/merge-train.yml. One run sweeps every
repository the merge-train app is installed on; the repositories it serves
keep no caller and no secret. The steps live in
.github/workflows/merge-train.yml of the shared repository, named here by
commit with the version as a comment (decision record 0029).

Before the first run, in the repository that keeps this caller: the
environment merge-train lets only the branch main deploy and holds the app's
private key as the secret MERGE_TRAIN_APP_KEY; the repository variable
MERGE_TRAIN_APP_CLIENT_ID holds the app's client id. The called job names the
environment, so a run from any other branch is refused before the key is
read. Without the key or the client id the run stops with exit code 3 and
writes nothing.

Runner: one of the fleet's own runners with python3 and openssl; the fleet
runs no hosted runner minutes for this.

Off switch: the variable MERGE_TRAIN set to `off` makes every run report only,
with read rights. Unset, the train runs.

Scopes: none. The called jobs write with the app's tokens, one per
repository, minted for that repository alone and revoked after it;
GITHUB_TOKEN gets no permission. After the sweep, a second called job runs
release-please in every repository with release-please-config.json and
.release-please-manifest.json on its default branch (decision record 0031);
it needs nothing more from this caller.

Required check: none. The job runs on a schedule and by hand, never on a pull
request, and is no check of a pull request (cordanaLLM/praetor#1212 for the
name the engine declares).

Triggers: every 20 minutes, off the top of the hour; one run lands or updates
at most one pull request in each repository. Dispatch is the manual nudge.
Concurrency keeps one run at a time and never cancels a run halfway.

Fields: .Shared.Repository, .Shared.Commit and .Shared.Version are working
names until the engine renders caller templates (cordanaLLM/praetor#1211);
.RunnerTag is the engine's own.

Licence header: the rendered caller starts with the consumer's own header,
written from .Licence (working names, as above), so the consumer's licence
check accepts it (#3). The REUSE-IgnoreStart and REUSE-IgnoreEnd notes render
as nothing and keep this repository's licence check from reading the field
lines as tags.
*/ -%>
<%- /* REUSE-IgnoreStart */ -%>
# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: <% .Licence.CopyrightText %>
# SPDX-License-Identifier: <% .Licence.Identifier %>
<%/* REUSE-IgnoreEnd */ -%>
---
# Merge train: in every repository of the merge-train app, lands one clean
# pull request or keeps the next one up to date. The job is the shared
# workflow of <% .Shared.Repository %>, named by commit.
name: Merge train

on:
  schedule:
    - cron: "7,27,47 * * * *"
  workflow_dispatch:

permissions: {}

concurrency:
  group: merge-train
  cancel-in-progress: false

jobs:
  train:
    name: Merge train
    permissions: {}
    uses: <% .Shared.Repository %>/.github/workflows/merge-train.yml@<% .Shared.Commit %> # <% .Shared.Version %>
    with:
      runner: <% .RunnerTag %>
      app_client_id: ${{ vars.MERGE_TRAIN_APP_CLIENT_ID }}
      switch: ${{ vars.MERGE_TRAIN || 'on' }}
    secrets:
      app_private_key: ${{ secrets.MERGE_TRAIN_APP_KEY }}
